@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `usca-general-provisions`
IMPORT `usca-deputies`

-- Tests of usca-deputies.l4 (Gov. Code §§ 7.5-7.9a).  Each expected value is decided from the section cited above the assertion, before the run.
-- The Constitution is not deposited, so whether a person holds a position specified in it is supplied as a fact.  A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `Gov. Code § 7.5: who a director may designate`

-- All three conditions: the director is by law a member of the body, the person is a deputy director of that department, and the person holds a position specified in (f) or (g).
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 7.5 lets the director designate` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 7.5 lets the director designate` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 7.5 lets the director designate` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 7.5 lets the director designate` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `Gov. Code § 7.5, § 7.6(a), § 7.8, § 7.9(a): what a designated deputy may do`

-- Each of the four acts the text names is open to a person designated under each of the four provisions.
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.5` TRUE `being counted in constituting a quorum`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.5` TRUE `participating in the proceedings`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.5` TRUE `voting upon any and all matters`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.5` TRUE `any other act the member could do if personally present`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.6` TRUE `being counted in constituting a quorum`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.6` TRUE `participating in the proceedings`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.6` TRUE `voting upon any and all matters`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.6` TRUE `any other act the member could do if personally present`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.8` TRUE `being counted in constituting a quorum`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.8` TRUE `participating in the proceedings`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.8` TRUE `voting upon any and all matters`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.8` TRUE `any other act the member could do if personally present`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.9(a)` TRUE `being counted in constituting a quorum`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.9(a)` TRUE `participating in the proceedings`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.9(a)` TRUE `voting upon any and all matters`
#ASSERT `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.9(a)` TRUE `any other act the member could do if personally present`
-- A person who was not designated under the provision has none of it.
#ASSERT NOT (`a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.5` FALSE `voting upon any and all matters`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.6` FALSE `voting upon any and all matters`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.8` FALSE `voting upon any and all matters`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `Section 7.9(a)` FALSE `voting upon any and all matters`)
-- A provision outside the four is not answered.
#ASSERT REFUSED `a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` `another provision` TRUE `voting upon any and all matters`

§ `Gov. Code § 7.5, § 7.6(a), § 7.8, § 7.9(a): the officer is responsible for the deputy's acts`

#ASSERT `the officer is responsible for the act of the deputy` `Section 7.5` TRUE `the same extent as for the deputy's official duties in the deputy's own post`
#ASSERT `the officer is responsible for the act of the deputy` `Section 7.6` TRUE `the same extent as for the deputy's official duties in the deputy's own post`
#ASSERT `the officer is responsible for the act of the deputy` `Section 7.8` TRUE `the same extent as for the deputy's official duties in the deputy's own post`
#ASSERT `the officer is responsible for the act of the deputy` `Section 7.9(a)` TRUE `the same extent as for the deputy's official duties in the deputy's own post`
-- The text makes the officer answerable to the same extent, no greater and no less.
#ASSERT NOT (`the officer is responsible for the act of the deputy` `Section 7.5` TRUE `a greater extent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the officer is responsible for the act of the deputy` `Section 7.5` TRUE `a lesser extent`)
-- An act the deputy did not do under the designation is not within what the section makes the officer answerable for.
#ASSERT NOT (`the officer is responsible for the act of the deputy` `Section 7.5` FALSE `the same extent as for the deputy's official duties in the deputy's own post`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the officer is responsible for the act of the deputy` `another provision` TRUE `the same extent as for the deputy's official duties in the deputy's own post`

§ `Gov. Code § 7.5 and § 7.8: how many directors may be represented at one meeting`

-- § 7.5: not more than one director.
#ASSERT `this many directors may be represented by deputies at a meeting under` `Section 7.5` `another state board, commission, committee or governing body` 0
#ASSERT `this many directors may be represented by deputies at a meeting under` `Section 7.5` `another state board, commission, committee or governing body` 1
#ASSERT NOT (`this many directors may be represented by deputies at a meeting under` `Section 7.5` `another state board, commission, committee or governing body` 2)
#ASSERT NOT (`this many directors may be represented by deputies at a meeting under` `Section 7.5` `another state board, commission, committee or governing body` 3)
-- § 7.8 lifts the limit for the State Allocation Board (fork F-7.8); for another body, or under another provision, the text does not say.
#ASSERT `this many directors may be represented by deputies at a meeting under` `Section 7.8` `the State Allocation Board` 3
#ASSERT REFUSED `this many directors may be represented by deputies at a meeting under` `Section 7.8` `another state board, commission, committee or governing body` 2
#ASSERT REFUSED `this many directors may be represented by deputies at a meeting under` `Section 7.6` `another state board, commission, committee or governing body` 2
#ASSERT REFUSED `this many directors may be represented by deputies at a meeting under` `another provision` `the State Allocation Board` 2
-- Fork F-7.8: whether more than one person may represent the same director is not answered.
#ASSERT `more persons may represent the same director at a meeting under Section 7.8` 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `more persons may represent the same director at a meeting under Section 7.8` 2

