§ `Gov. Code § 7.6(d): the Attorney General`

#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 7.6(d) lets the Attorney General designate` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 7.6(d) lets the Attorney General designate` FALSE)
-- On a body of which the Attorney General is presiding officer the designee may not preside; the text does not speak of any other body.
#ASSERT NOT (`a person designated by the Attorney General may act as presiding officer in the Attorney General's place` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `a person designated by the Attorney General may act as presiding officer in the Attorney General's place` FALSE

