§ `Gov. Code § 7.7: Sections 7.5 and 7.6 do not affect Section 7`

#ASSERT NOT (`the section affects or modifies Section 7` `Section 7.5`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the section affects or modifies Section 7` `Section 7.6`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the section affects or modifies Section 7` `another section`
-- So Section 7 still lets the officer's deputy exercise a power of the officer, as the pass-1 function reads it, whatever §§ 7.5 and 7.6 let a director or a constitutional officer do.
#ASSERT `a power of a public officer may be exercised, or a duty performed, by` `a deputy of the officer` `given that` FALSE

§ `Gov. Code § 7.8: the State Allocation Board`

#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 7.8 lets the director designate` `the Director of Finance` `the State Allocation Board` TRUE
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 7.8 lets the director designate` `the Director of General Services` `the State Allocation Board` TRUE
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 7.8 lets the director designate` `the Director of Education` `the State Allocation Board` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 7.8 lets the director designate` `the Controller` `the State Allocation Board` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 7.8 lets the director designate` `the Attorney General` `the State Allocation Board` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 7.8 lets the director designate` `an office the text does not name` `the State Allocation Board` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 7.8 lets the director designate` `the Director of Finance` `the State Board of Education` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 7.8 lets the director designate` `the Director of Finance` `the State Allocation Board` FALSE)
-- 'Irrespective of whether said deputy or assistant director holds a position specified in subdivision (g)': a deputy director with no such position is outside § 7.5 and inside § 7.8.
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 7.5 lets the director designate` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 7.8 lets the director designate` `the Director of Finance` `the State Allocation Board` TRUE

